occurrences.sourceExplanation:
Value stream management is not a step in value stream mapping. Value stream mapping includes the following steps:
1. value stream identification;
2. mapping of the ‘as-is’ value stream;
3. analysing the value stream;
4. mapping a ‘to-be’ value stream;
5. planning and implementing improvements. Value stream management is used to maintain high quality of services and continually optimize the flow of work, which means both ‘management of value streams’ and ‘management through value streams’.
